-- ── H4 dispatch generalization — CONFIRMED ──
-- join_extensional now computes Option<BaseDispatch> from the leg and selects
-- every set-at-once phase (anti-join set, attr value-generator, cached free
-- generators, build-once) by (strategy, arity, order) + the leg's bound mask;
-- join_edge_generator_cached / join_edge_bound_built_once take EdgeOrder (the
-- `name == "incoming"` matches deleted); build_anti_join_set takes &LegSource;
-- join_base_against resolves its eval through base_dispatch_parts. The
-- type→node alias (exec.rs old :1958/:1710) and the incoming string-matches are
-- deleted; `incoming` legs arrive as (edge_id, SortOrder::Reverse) — pinned by
-- exec::tests::incoming_leg_is_edge_reverse_run (plan-level dispatch equality +
-- output equality vs the endpoint-swapped edge leg under BOTH min_rows 0 and
-- usize::MAX). edge_attr keeps an explicitly documented builtin-side arm
-- (spec Q2's allowed form). Emission byte-identity: the pre-existing A/B
-- multiset battery (with_build_once_min_rows 0 vs usize::MAX, incl. its
-- incoming leg e_in) green over the migrated dispatch; per-row eval remains the
-- correctness floor.
claim_of[a](r_p3_dispatch_keyed_id_order_mask).
ground[a](r_p3_dispatch_keyed_id_order_mask, ab_battery_green_incoming_equals_edge_reverse).

